**U66 (descriptive). Among OECD members Australia is near the top for filings from abroad and new businesses, and near
the bottom for exports, manufacturing and business R&D.**
- **Top:** new businesses registered (2nd of 30; 316,561 in 2024), non-resident patent applications (5th of 38;
  27,945 against a median member's 425), non-resident trade mark classes (5th of 34), new business density (4th of 30;
  18.06 per 1,000 people aged 15 to 64, median 5.83) and tertiary enrolment (4th of 22).
- **Bottom:** exports of goods and services (34th of 35; 23.24% of GDP, median 45.37%), manufacturing (31st of 32;
  5.32%, median 12.79%), business R&D (26th of 35; 0.91% of GDP, median 1.18%) and gross R&D (21st of 35; 1.68%,
  median 1.85%).
- **Counts rank by size:** Australia's population is 14th of 38 and its GDP 13th, so its counts of filings, articles
  and royalties sit around the 60th to 75th percentile for that reason alone.
